  "body": "Context: [Chrome Status: User Agent Launch Type in PerformanceNavigationTiming](https://chromestatus.com/feature/5186950448283648?context=myfeatures)\r\n\r\nWhile discussing extending the PerformanceNavigationTiming structure to distinguish between 'warm start' and 'cold start' scenarios, it was [mentioned](https://github.com/w3c/navigation-timing/issues/180#issuecomment-1151717823) that the `NavigationType` enumeration maps 1:1 to the historyHandling type in the HTML specification.\r\n\r\nIn our Explainer for this feature, we have a [proposal](https://github.com/MicrosoftEdge/MSEdgeExplainers/blob/main/PerformanceNavigationTiming%20for%20User%20Agent%20Launch/explainer.md#mapping-to-html-historyhandling-definition) to include 'launch' as a valid option for historyHandling.\r\n\r\nI'm not sure if this is the _correct_ way to map this concept, so I'm looking for your feedback on how to best approach this!",
